# Copy this file to .env and fill in the provider(s) you want mapd chat /
# mapd fix / mapd mcp to use. mapd loads .env automatically (no restart or
# extra flag needed) — it never overwrites a variable you've already exported
# in your shell. Two places you can put it, checked in this order:
#
#   1. <your-project>/.env   — applies only to that project, overrides #2
#   2. ~/.env (home dir)     — applies to EVERY project as a fallback
#
# Put your key in ~/.env once and it works everywhere; only add a project's
# own .env if that project needs a different key/model than your default.
#
# You only need ONE provider below. With none set, mapd runs fully in
# deterministic mode (no chat Q&A, no `mapd fix --propose`, but everything
# else works).

# Anthropic (Claude)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# OpenAI-compatible
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# Kimi (Moonshot AI) — OpenAI-compatible, its own key so it never collides
# with a real OpenAI key set at the same time.
# KIMI_API_KEY=sk-...
# KIMI_BASE_URL=https://api.moonshot.ai/v1
